      "procedure": "Limit of cis-isomer (USP <621>): mobile phase = 100 mL isopropyl alcohol + 1 mL glacial acetic acid, diluted with hexane to 1 L. System suitability stock: 1 mg USP Glimepiride Related Compound A RS in 1 mL methylene chloride + 3 mL mobile phase. System suitability solution: 10 mg USP Glimepiride RS in 20 mL flask, dissolve in 5 mL methylene chloride, dilute with mobile phase to volume; transfer 5 mL to a separate flask, add 50 µL stock, mix. Sample solution: 10 mg glimepiride in 20 mL flask, dissolve in 5 mL methylene chloride, dilute with mobile phase to volume. Column 3 mm x 15 cm, 5 µm L20; UV 228 nm; 0.5 mL/min; 10 µL. Suitability: S/N NLT 15 for cis-isomer peak; peak-to-valley ratio NLT 2.0. Result % = rcis / (rcis + rG) x 100. NMT 0.8%.",
